Based on a patch originally written by Benjamin Tissoires.

Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org   # v3.2+
Signed-off-by: Nestor Lopez Casado <nlopezcasad@logitech.com>
Signed-off-by: Jiri Kosina <jkosina@suse.cz>

Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by a race condition introduced after a previous commit, which led to the `hid-core` discarding incoming packets while the HID driver's probe function was executing. This resulted in the loss of control packets necessary for the enumeration process of the Logitech Unifying device, as these packets must be received in conjunction with mouse and keyboard packets. When control packets were discarded, the driver could not properly recognize paired devices, leading to the issue of missing devices.

